{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790349544,"nonce":"V0me2oLQlJfJ+c3vFj/UHo1zbac=","title":"zyntax compile cannot AOT-build a ZynML program: its grammar path skips imports, builtins and impl registration","message":"`zyntax compile --backend llvm -g crates/zynml/ml.zyn -s prog.zynml -o prog`, the AOT route the book documents, fails for every ZynML program that imports the prelude, and for prelude-free programs that read a field of a user struct or call a method. ZynML itself has no AOT command (`zynml` has run, watch, parse, repl, check), so this is the only route.\n\nThe cause is that load_grammar2 (crates/zyntax_cli/src/formats/zyn_grammar.rs:134) lowers through the CLI's own lower_to_hir (:461) instead of the pipeline every runtime uses (zyntax_embed's lower_typed_program, public as TieredRuntime::lower_to_hir, crates/zyntax_embed/src/runtime/tiered.rs:1623):\n\n- Imports are never resolved. build_import_context's result (crates/zyntax_cli/src/commands.rs:125) is built and dropped, and ZynML's stdlib lives in its snapshot, which the CLI never installs. `println(42)` fails with \"Call to undefined function 'println'\".\n- The grammar's @builtin aliases and the plugins' signatures are not passed (LoweringConfig::default() at zyn_grammar.rs:544). An f-string call that does reach a `$IO$...` extern gets no DynamicBox boxing.\n- A struct that Grammar2 pre-registered as a field-less placeholder is skipped as \"already registered\" (zyn_grammar.rs:472) instead of filled in: \"Field 'x' not found in type 'Body' (has: )\". Impl blocks are never registered and unresolved types never resolved: \"Cannot call methods on non-nominal type: Unresolved(..)\", \"Method 'check' not found\".\n- A function that fails analysis is dropped with a warn-level log (crates/compiler/src/lowering.rs:2681), which the CLI does not show, so the failure surfaces somewhere else: \"undefined reference to `main'\" from the linker, or \"Call to undefined function 'bench'\" in the caller.\n\nReproducer: crates/zynml/examples/test_02_println_int.zynml. `zynml run` prints 42, -10, 0; the zyntax compile line above fails with the undefined-println error. None of 31 prelude-importing programs produces an executable (examples test_01 to test_12, hello, collections, tensor_ops, compute_simd, trait_method, and the bench kernels wrapped to print): 27 stop at the undefined println, two at a for over a List that `zynml run` refuses as well, test_09_for_loop in LLVM codegen because the unknown println inside a for body becomes an indirect call (457bd98), and test_11_fstring_number compiles and fails to link (36aa93b). With the prelude import removed and output through an `extern def putchar`, arithmetic, control flow, recursion, counted for loops and floats build, link and match `zynml run`; nbody, method_call, op_overload and binary_trees still fail as above. Mac arm64 and NUC x86_64, main 19697230 plus the entry-name fix on branch aot-reval.\n\nFix direction: AOT lowers through the embed pipeline with the language's snapshot and plugins installed, then hands the module to the LLVM object writer. For ZynML that is a `zynml build` (or a CLI mode that takes a runtime's lowering); the CLI's own lower_to_hir then goes. The test crates/zyntax_cli/tests/llvm_aot_zynml.rs (branch aot-reval) carries ignored cases for this.","files":null}]}